<title>SOUTH KOREA: SEOULBANK shares down on probe news.</title>
<headline>SEOULBANK shares down on probe news.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in SEOULBANK fell 1.75 percent, or 80 won, to 4,490 on Friday on news that the bank's president has been questioned on charges of taking bribes, brokers said.  </p>
<p>SEOULBANK's spokesman Koh Myoung-il denied the Korean Broadcasting System (KBS) report that the bank's president Sohn Hong-gyun has been under investigation.</p>
<p>The state radio KBS said South Korean prosecutors have questioned Sohn on allegations that he took bribes from two to three companies in return for help in getting loans approved.</p>
<p>SEOULBANK briefly fell to this year's lowest level of 4,480 won before recovering to end the morning session at 4,490.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
